			"notes": "Hey folks! Sorry about the long delay for the 1.21.3 build; I happened to have been working on something **BIG!** There is something for everyone in this update, but datapack developers are especially in for a field day.\n\n## ➕ Additions\nNote block instruments are now data-driven! Yes, really! The `instrument` block state property has been entirely replaced with a new implementation taking advantage of json data files. You should be able to add your very own instruments with just a little bit of fiddling. Datapack-ers: stay tuned for an upcoming wiki page here on GitHub.\n\nThere's a new config option on the block! Located in the config path `Behaviors > Inputs > Keyboard Layout`, this allows **Glissando** keybind inputs to work with certain regional keyboard structures. It defaults to `QWERTY` but `ÄWERTY`, `AZERTY`, `QÜERTY` and `QWERTZ` are also supported at this time.\n\n> [!NOTE]  \n> It's not hard for me to add new keyboard layouts. If your keyboard layout isn't supported, drop an issue report and I'll get to it in the next update!\n\n## 🔧 Changes\n![New Glissando tooltips](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75a1f1db-b8a0-484a-bf96-92cb81cb5cd9)\n\nTooltips have been redesigned to be more similar to various others present throughout the game. Some notable specifics:\n- The line \"Press [char] or click to play\" (previously \"Press [char] to play\") is now treated as a title. You cannot move this line underneath the others and you cannot remove it without hiding the entire tooltip via the config option `Visuals > Tooltips > Enabled`. It is now the only line to recolor when the config option `Visuals > Tooltips > Title Colors` is enabled, previously just `Colors`.\n- The `Note` and `Pitch` lines are still toggleable except they have moved to their own config group, `Visuals > Tooltip Line Arrangement`. Here, you can shuffle the order in which these lines appear or even hide them entirely.\n\nTechnical players like myself have a tendency to use note block-observer circuits as buttons since they only have 4 ticks of cooldown and they're much easier to hit. The initial release of **Glissando** made this impossible; you either open the screen or skip the action if the note block is invalid. This update semi-fixes this issue by allowing the `note` block state property to cycle when the note block screen cannot be opened. Practically, this just means your buttons now must have blocks on top!\n\n## ➖ Removals\n`Behaviors > Keybind Inputs > Enabled` and `Mouse Inputs > Enabled` have been removed. It didn't feel right to be able to disable certain input methods. If you don't want to use your keyboard, just like... don't, xD\n\n## 🐛 Fixes\n- Clicking the top face of a note block that has a top instrument resting on it (e.g. a creeper head) while holding a top instrument in your hand now correctly plays the note block instead of skipping the action. This is a bug from vanilla **Minecraft**."
		},
